    "body": "Follow-up to #36663. These two pre-existing nits came up in review there and were left out of that PR to avoid review churn ([comment](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36663#issuecomment-6515191239)).\n\nRemove the \"Generate a block\" log line in `test_reorg`. It adds nothing and causes confusion. The log line above it already says \"Broadcast and mine spend_3_1\" and the mining only happens a few lines later in `self.generate(self.nodes[0], FORK_LENGTH - 1)`.\n\nUpdate the comment \"Create a child of that transaction\" in `test_reorg_relay`. It sits right below `tx_before_reorg`, so it suggests the child spends `tx_before_reorg`. The child actually spends `tx_disconnected`, so name it explicitly.\n\nOnly a log message and a comment change, so test behavior is unchanged. `mempool_reorg.py` passes locally.",
